From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:50:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: Give the CPU thermal zone usable trips
 and cooling maps

The H616 cpu-thermal zone was modelled on the vendor BSP's layout for
the power allocator governor: a 60 degC "threshold" trip and a 70 degC
"target" trip, plus sustainable-power. Mainline however has no way to
select a governor from DT, there is no energy model for the H616 CPUs,
and the zone has no cooling-maps at all. The result is that the two
passive trips only switch the zone to fast polling, nothing ever
throttles the CPU, and the only protection is the 110 degC critical
shutdown. The vendor BSP itself (sun50iw9.dtsi) uses 70/90 degC and
does map cpu_target to the CPUs.

Follow the H6 (same Cortex-A53 cluster, same thermal sensor family)
convention for step_wise instead:

 - passive "cpu-alert" at 85 degC with 2 degC hysteresis, mapped to all
   four CPUs with THERMAL_NO_LIMIT. This is the value mainline uses for
   the H6, 5 degC below the vendor BSP's own 90 degC throttling target
   and 25 degC below the 110 degC the vendor treats as the shutdown
   temperature, while far above the ~60 degC an Orange Pi Zero2 reaches
   at 1.5 GHz under sustained load, so normal operation is never
   throttled;
 - a "cpu-hot" trip at 100 degC for monitoring/notification;
 - keep the existing 110 degC critical trip (vendor value).

sustainable-power is kept so the zone can still be driven by the power
allocator once an energy model is described.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi | 30 +++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -1838,20 +1838,32 @@
 			sustainable-power = <1000>;
 
 			trips {
-				cpu_threshold: cpu-trip-0 {
-					temperature = <60000>;
+				cpu_alert: cpu-alert {
+					temperature = <85000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
 					type = "passive";
-					hysteresis = <0>;
 				};
-				cpu_target: cpu-trip-1 {
-					temperature = <70000>;
-					type = "passive";
-					hysteresis = <0>;
+
+				cpu_hot: cpu-hot {
+					temperature = <100000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "hot";
 				};
-				cpu_critical: cpu-trip-2 {
+
+				cpu_critical: cpu-crit {
 					temperature = <110000>;
-					type = "critical";
 					hysteresis = <0>;
+					type = "critical";
+				};
+			};
+
+			cooling-maps {
+				map0 {
+					trip = <&cpu_alert>;
+					cooling-device = <&cpu0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+							 <&cpu1 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+							 <&cpu2 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+							 <&cpu3 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
 				};
 			};
 		};
